Relevant columns and how they will be used  

Targetome – interactions_v1  
• drugName / drugID : find the rows that correspond to the drug “sorafenib”.  
• targetID / targetName / target_uniprotID / targetSpecies : identify the Homo sapiens targets of sorafenib.  
• expID : tie every interaction to its experimental evidence so that potency filters can be applied.  

Targetome – experiments_v1  
• expID : join key to interactions_v1.  
• exp_assayValueMedian, exp_assayValueLow, exp_assayValueHigh : apply the potency filter (median ≤ 100 AND (low ≤ 100 OR NULL) AND (high ≤ 100 OR NULL)).  
• exp_assayUnits : make sure the assay is expressed in the same units (usually nM).  

Reactome – physical_entity_v77  
• uniprot_id : join to the sorafenib targets’ UniProt IDs.  
• stable_id : Reactome physical‑entity identifier used in the next join.  

Reactome – pe_to_pathway_v77  
• pe_stable_id : join to physical_entity_v77.stable_id.  
• pathway_stable_id : the pathway where the entity is found.  
• evidence_code : keep only rows with evidence_code = 'TAS'.  

Reactome – pathway_v77  
• stable_id : join key.  
• species : keep only “Homo sapiens”.  
• lowest_level : keep only TRUE (lowest‑level pathways).  
• name : report the pathway’s common name.  

(For the χ² contingency table we will later need the total set of Homo sapiens physical entities with TAS evidence, so we can decide whether a physical entity is “inside” or “outside” a given pathway.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Exploratory & building‑block queries  
Each query is limited to 20 rows; all tables come from the public project isb‑cgc‑bq.  
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1.  List all distinct drug names that contain the word “sorafenib”.
SELECT DISTINCT drugID, drugName
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1`
WHERE  LOWER(drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  Retrieve all Homo sapiens targets of sorafenib (no potency filter yet).
SELECT DISTINCT i.targetID,
       i.targetName,
       i.target_uniprotID
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
WHERE  LOWER(i.drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
  AND  i.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Add the experimental evidence and apply the potency threshold (≤ 100 nM).
SELECT DISTINCT i.targetID,
       i.targetName,
       i.target_uniprotID,
       e.exp_assayValueLow,
       e.exp_assayValueMedian,
       e.exp_assayValueHigh
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`  AS e
       ON i.expID = e.expID
WHERE  LOWER(i.drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
  AND  i.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'
  AND  e.exp_assayUnits = 'nM'
  AND  e.exp_assayValueMedian <= 100
  AND  (e.exp_assayValueLow   <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueLow   IS NULL)
  AND  (e.exp_assayValueHigh  <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueHigh  IS NULL)
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Map the filtered targets to Reactome physical_entity stable IDs.
SELECT DISTINCT p.stable_id            AS pe_stable_id,
       p.uniprot_id,
       p.name                          AS pe_name
FROM (
      -- subquery = potency‑filtered sorafenib targets
      SELECT DISTINCT i.target_uniprotID
      FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
      JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`  AS e
             ON i.expID = e.expID
      WHERE  LOWER(i.drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
        AND  i.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'
        AND  e.exp_assayUnits = 'nM'
        AND  e.exp_assayValueMedian <= 100
        AND  (e.exp_assayValueLow  <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueLow  IS NULL)
        AND  (e.exp_assayValueHigh <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueHigh IS NULL)
     ) AS t
JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
       ON t.target_uniprotID = p.uniprot_id
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5.  Attach TAS pathways to the physical entities just obtained.
SELECT DISTINCT pep.pe_stable_id,
       ppv.pathway_stable_id
FROM (
      SELECT DISTINCT p.stable_id AS pe_stable_id
      FROM (
            -- potency‑filtered sorafenib targets (same as Query 4)
            SELECT DISTINCT i.target_uniprotID
            FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
            JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`  AS e
                   ON i.expID = e.expID
            WHERE  LOWER(i.drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
              AND  i.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'
              AND  e.exp_assayUnits = 'nM'
              AND  e.exp_assayValueMedian <= 100
              AND  (e.exp_assayValueLow  <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueLow  IS NULL)
              AND  (e.exp_assayValueHigh <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueHigh IS NULL)
           ) AS tg
      JOIN `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
            ON tg.target_uniprotID = p.uniprot_id
     ) AS pep
JOIN `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77` AS ppv
     ON pep.pe_stable_id = ppv.pe_stable_id
WHERE ppv.evidence_code = 'TAS'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Keep only mapping to lowest‑level Homo sapiens pathways.
SELECT DISTINCT ppv.pathway_stable_id,
       pv.name AS pathway_name
FROM `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77` AS ppv
JOIN `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pathway_v77`        AS pv
     ON ppv.pathway_stable_id = pv.stable_id
WHERE ppv.evidence_code = 'TAS'
  AND pv.species       = 'Homo sapiens'
  AND pv.lowest_level  = TRUE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  Count how many sorafenib targets (potency‑filtered) are found in each
--     lowest‑level Homo sapiens pathway with TAS evidence.
WITH soraf_targets AS (
      -- physical entities of potency‑filtered sorafenib targets
      SELECT DISTINCT p.stable_id AS pe_stable_id
      FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
      JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`  AS e
             ON i.expID = e.expID
      JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
             ON i.target_uniprotID = p.uniprot_id
      WHERE  LOWER(i.drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
        AND  i.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'
        AND  e.exp_assayUnits = 'nM'
        AND  e.exp_assayValueMedian <= 100
        AND  (e.exp_assayValueLow  <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueLow  IS NULL)
        AND  (e.exp_assayValueHigh <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueHigh IS NULL)
), path_map AS (
      SELECT pe_stable_id,
             pathway_stable_id
      FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77`
      WHERE  evidence_code = 'TAS'
)
SELECT pm.pathway_stable_id,
       COUNT(DISTINCT pm.pe_stable_id) AS num_soraf_targets
FROM   path_map AS pm
JOIN   soraf_targets AS st
       ON pm.pe_stable_id = st.pe_stable_id
JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pathway_v77` AS pv
       ON pm.pathway_stable_id = pv.stable_id
WHERE  pv.species      = 'Homo sapiens'
  AND  pv.lowest_level = TRUE
GROUP BY pm.pathway_stable_id
ORDER BY num_soraf_targets DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8.  Count the total number of TAS physical entities inside each
--     lowest‑level pathway (needed for χ² denominator).
SELECT pm.pathway_stable_id,
       COUNT(DISTINCT pm.pe_stable_id) AS total_entities_in_pathway
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77` AS pm
JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pathway_v77`       AS pv
       ON pm.pathway_stable_id = pv.stable_id
WHERE  pm.evidence_code = 'TAS'
  AND  pv.species       = 'Homo sapiens'
  AND  pv.lowest_level  = TRUE
GROUP BY pm.pathway_stable_id
ORDER BY total_entities_in_pathway DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9.  Build the 2×2 contingency components for every pathway:
--     a = targets in pathway
--     b = targets NOT in pathway
--     c = non‑targets in pathway
--     d = non‑targets NOT in pathway
WITH soraf_targets AS (
      SELECT DISTINCT p.stable_id AS pe_stable_id
      FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
      JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`  AS e
             ON i.expID = e.expID
      JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
             ON i.target_uniprotID = p.uniprot_id
      WHERE  LOWER(i.drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
        AND  i.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'
        AND  e.exp_assayUnits = 'nM'
        AND  e.exp_assayValueMedian <= 100
        AND  (e.exp_assayValueLow  <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueLow  IS NULL)
        AND  (e.exp_assayValueHigh <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueHigh IS NULL)
), tas_map AS (
      SELECT pe_stable_id,
             pathway_stable_id
      FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77`
      WHERE  evidence_code = 'TAS'
), lowest_human_paths AS (
      SELECT stable_id
      FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pathway_v77`
      WHERE  species = 'Homo sapiens'
        AND  lowest_level = TRUE
)
SELECT p.stable_id                           AS pathway_id,
       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN st.pe_stable_id IS NOT NULL THEN tas.pe_stable_id END) AS a_targets_in,
       COUNT(DISTINCT st.pe_stable_id) -
       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN st.pe_stable_id IS NOT NULL THEN tas.pe_stable_id END) AS b_targets_out,
       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN st.pe_stable_id IS NULL THEN tas.pe_stable_id END)     AS c_nontargets_in,
       (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT pe_stable_id)
        FROM   tas_map) 
       - COUNT(DISTINCT st.pe_stable_id)
       - COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN st.pe_stable_id IS NULL THEN tas.pe_stable_id END)
       AS d_nontargets_out
FROM   lowest_human_paths AS p
LEFT JOIN tas_map AS tas
       ON p.stable_id = tas.pathway_stable_id
LEFT JOIN soraf_targets AS st
       ON tas.pe_stable_id = st.pe_stable_id
GROUP BY p.stable_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10.  Compute χ² for every pathway and output the three highest values.
WITH soraf_targets AS (
      SELECT DISTINCT p.stable_id AS pe_stable_id
      FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
      JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`  AS e
             ON i.expID = e.expID
      JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
             ON i.target_uniprotID = p.uniprot_id
      WHERE  LOWER(i.drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
        AND  i.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'
        AND  e.exp_assayUnits = 'nM'
        AND  e.exp_assayValueMedian <= 100
        AND  (e.exp_assayValueLow  <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueLow  IS NULL)
        AND  (e.exp_assayValueHigh <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueHigh IS NULL)
), tas_map AS (
      SELECT pe_stable_id,
             pathway_stable_id
      FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77`
      WHERE  evidence_code = 'TAS'
), lowest_human_paths AS (
      SELECT stable_id, name
      FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pathway_v77`
      WHERE  species = 'Homo sapiens'
        AND  lowest_level = TRUE
), totals AS (
      SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT pe_stable_id) AS total_pe
      FROM   tas_map
)
SELECT p.stable_id                AS pathway_id,
       p.name                     AS pathway_name,
       a_targets_in,
       b_targets_out,
       c_nontargets_in,
       d_nontargets_out,
       -- χ² = Σ (O‑E)² / E ;  here we compute it in a 2×2 contingency
       (
         (POW(a_targets_in -
              ( (a_targets_in + b_targets_out) *
                (a_targets_in + c_nontargets_in) /
                (a_targets_in + b_targets_out + c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out)
               ), 2)
          /
              ( (a_targets_in + b_targets_out) *
                (a_targets_in + c_nontargets_in) /
                (a_targets_in + b_targets_out + c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out)
              )
         )
         +
         (POW(b_targets_out -
              ( (a_targets_in + b_targets_out) *
                (b_targets_out + d_nontargets_out) /
                (a_targets_in + b_targets_out + c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out)
               ), 2)
          /
              ( (a_targets_in + b_targets_out) *
                (b_targets_out + d_nontargets_out) /
                (a_targets_in + b_targets_out + c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out)
              )
         )
         +
         (POW(c_nontargets_in -
              ( (c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out) *
                (a_targets_in + c_nontargets_in) /
                (a_targets_in + b_targets_out + c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out)
               ), 2)
          /
              ( (c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out) *
                (a_targets_in + c_nontargets_in) /
                (a_targets_in + b_targets_out + c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out)
              )
         )
         +
         (POW(d_nontargets_out -
              ( (c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out) *
                (b_targets_out + d_nontargets_out) /
                (a_targets_in + b_targets_out + c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out)
               ), 2)
          /
              ( (c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out) *
                (b_targets_out + d_nontargets_out) /
                (a_targets_in + b_targets_out + c_nontargets_in + d_nontargets_out)
              )
         )
       ) AS chi_squared
FROM (
      -- build the four cells a, b, c, d
      SELECT p.stable_id,
             COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN st.pe_stable_id IS NOT NULL THEN tas.pe_stable_id END) AS a_targets_in,
             COUNT(DISTINCT st.pe_stable_id) -
             COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN st.pe_stable_id IS NOT NULL THEN tas.pe_stable_id END) AS b_targets_out,
             COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN st.pe_stable_id IS NULL THEN tas.pe_stable_id END)     AS c_nontargets_in,
             (SELECT total_pe FROM totals) -
             COUNT(DISTINCT st.pe_stable_id) -
             COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN st.pe_stable_id IS NULL THEN tas.pe_stable_id END)     AS d_nontargets_out
      FROM   lowest_human_paths AS p
      LEFT JOIN tas_map AS tas
             ON p.stable_id = tas.pathway_stable_id
      LEFT JOIN soraf_targets AS st
             ON tas.pe_stable_id = st.pe_stable_id
      GROUP BY p.stable_id
) AS table4
JOIN lowest_human_paths AS p
  ON p.stable_id = table4.stable_id
ORDER BY chi_squared DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

Each successive query adds complexity, leading up to query 10, which generates the three lowest‑level Homo sapiens pathways (with TAS evidence) that display the highest χ² statistics, together with the four cell counts needed for interpretation.
