Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  

Targetome – interactions_v1  
• drugName / drugID : find the rows that correspond to the drug “sorafenib”.  
• targetID / targetName / target_uniprotID / targetSpecies : identify the Homo sapiens targets of sorafenib.  
• expID : tie every interaction to its experimental evidence so that potency filters can be applied.  

Targetome – experiments_v1  
• expID : join key to interactions_v1.  
• exp_assayValueMedian, exp_assayValueLow, exp_assayValueHigh : apply the potency filter (median ≤ 100 AND (low ≤ 100 OR NULL) AND (high ≤ 100 OR NULL)).  
• exp_assayUnits : make sure the assay is expressed in the same units (usually nM).  

Reactome – physical_entity_v77  
• uniprot_id : join to the sorafenib targets’ UniProt IDs.  
• stable_id : Reactome physical‑entity identifier used in the next join.  

Reactome – pe_to_pathway_v77  
• pe_stable_id : join to physical_entity_v77.stable_id.  
• pathway_stable_id : the pathway where the entity is found.  
• evidence_code : keep only rows with evidence_code = 'TAS'.  

Reactome – pathway_v77  
• stable_id : join key.  
• species : keep only “Homo sapiens”.  
• lowest_level : keep only TRUE (lowest‑level pathways).  
• name : report the pathway’s common name.  

(For the χ² contingency table we will later need the total set of Homo sapiens physical entities with TAS evidence, so we can decide whether a physical entity is “inside” or “outside” a given pathway.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Exploratory & building‑block queries  
Each query is limited to 20 rows; all tables come from the public project isb‑cgc‑bq.  
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1.  List all distinct drug names that contain the word “sorafenib”.
SELECT DISTINCT drugID, drugName
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1`
WHERE  LOWER(drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  Retrieve all Homo sapiens targets of sorafenib (no potency filter yet).
SELECT DISTINCT i.targetID,
       i.targetName,
       i.target_uniprotID
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
WHERE  LOWER(i.drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
  AND  i.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Add the experimental evidence and apply the potency threshold (≤ 100 nM).
SELECT DISTINCT i.targetID,
       i.targetName,
       i.target_uniprotID,
       e.exp_assayValueLow,
       e.exp_assayValueMedian,
       e.exp_assayValueHigh
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`  AS e
       ON i.expID = e.expID
WHERE  LOWER(i.drugName) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
  AND  i.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'
  AND  e.exp_assayUnits = 'nM'
  AND  e.exp_assayValueMedian <= 100
  AND  (e.exp_assayValueLow   <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueLow   IS NULL)
  AND  (e.exp_assayValueHigh  <= 100 OR e.exp_assayValueHigh  IS NULL)
LIMIT  20;
